                                                "sense_id": "859fa032-e1c6-30f8-a915-d5ba0de17dd5",
                                                "text": "It worked through from Swindon with a test train of 16 coaches and the new W.R. dynamometer car, the whole totalling 571 tons; this is one of the heaviest trains ever worked by a single-handed locomotive over the South Devon banks—in fact, it was competently restarted from a test stop on Dainton bank."
